   i had the same "problem": the aha-2940-controller is not supported
   by srm. the only one that worked was a simple ncr-810 (pci).

   since srm doesn't find your harddisk(s) on the aha-2940, you cannot
   boot from an scsi-disk. but you could put in some ide-hd, boot from
   that disk (secondary boot-loader) and let all software reside on
   your scsi-disk. that should work because linux recognizes you
   adaptec-controller and so you can work with the scsi-disks.


