X-Complaints-To: newsmaster@saunalahti.fi

First of all, SRM did not want to touch this ATI device.  I do not
have the first serial port connected into anything at the moment so I
do not know what it says.  However it continues booting into MILO
after thinking for a good while, maybe two or three minutes.  I think
it did not take that much time with the Trident I have been using.
Trident also showed SRM console on screen.  With ATI, screen stays
completely dark until MILO gets loaded from floppy and initializes it.
From that point on boot continues normally.

This ATI graphics adapter seems to work well on X and console, except
for causing problem with keyboard.  After a while of uptime,
keypresses start getting lost somewhere.  I have to press keys about
one to ten times when trying to type something or move text cursor.
Switching between virtual terminals still works fine when this problem
shows up, just like it did with my Trident 8900D ISA graphics adapter.

Does anyone have ideas about how to get rid of that problem?  Feels
like graphics adapter would somehow manage to keep part of kernel busy
or manage to catch certain kind of keyboard events and make them to
disappear.  I bought this card just for the fun of testing, and might
just trade it for something else if I cannot get it to behave well
enough.  I can still keep running X on my SPARCstations.

I had to reboot many times since DE100 network adapter refused to work
with ATI installed.  This got solved by moving DE100 from default
setting of "mem=0xd0000" (autoprobing) to "mem=0xe0000" (manual
settings).  I also eliminated the problem of having to wait for SRM by
booting straight into MILO instead of going through first SRM.  MILO
gets loaded as "failsafe boot" from floppy.

Xfree identifies this ATI adapter as: 

 PCI: Mach64 Rage XL or XC rev 39, 
 Aperture @ 0x05000000, 
 Registers @ 0x06000000, 
 Block I/O @ 0x8800

Packaging material says:

 ATI XPERT98 PRO 8MB PCI

MILO version is 2.0.35-c7b, SRM version is... whatever is latest for
AXPpci.  Rest of the system is Debian GNU/Linux 2.2.

