Hello,

I am currently developing an rpm-based distriution of the 
self-optimizing linear algebra software ATLAS 
(http://www.netlib.org/atlas). Since ATLAS' optimizations
are very strongly architecture-dependent, I need to analyze
information from /proc/cpuinfo in the build process.

Unfortunately the format of /proc/cpuinfo seems to be 
different for different architectures, so I need to parse
for different fields depending on architecture.

To make the package portable, I'd therefore need sample
/proc/cpuinfos from recent Linux kernels on powerpc, m68k,
alpha, sparc,... architectures. Myself I've only access 
to Intel-based Linux machines, except for an Alpha EV6/7 
machine that I used at Compaq testdrive.

Thus, I'd be grateful to anybody who sends me an excerpt
of his /proc/cpuinfo, together with uname -a output and
a short description of his or her machine.

Martin

