Because you got the message "unable to mount root on 08:02" that means
that your kernel was properly loaded.
Because it says "08:02" I know that it really and truly did attempt the
second partition of the first scsi drive.  08 means the first scsi bus,
and 02 means second partition of the first hard drive.

You need to know the correct device... /dev/sda1 /dev/sda2 ... whatever.
If it's on sda, there are only 8 possibilities, and you already have
eliminated one of them.  You can guess and check.  Or you can get a rescue
floppy (or CD) and find out the correct partition and correct device name.



