Your CD is IDE, it's hda.

The boot for a serial install is

boot dqa0 -fl kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/hda console=ttyS0 expert
text"
you do not have to set the speed, the defaults are correct...

After  your install is done, you will still not be able to use the system
unless you also edit
/etc/inittab, /etc/securetty , /etc/aboot.conf

inittab you have to add a mingetty for ttyS0, so you can get a login prompt.
securetty, you have to add ttyS0 to be able to login as root..
aboot.conf,  add console=ttyS0, after the root command, to select a serial
console.

JJ

