Glad to help.
If you want a graphical display for configuration, might I suggest using a terminal
x-connection.  There are (as far as I know) no free X-servers for Windows, but many
have free evaluation periods.

If you use XDMCP (that's a specific X-windows protocol) you will have the graphical
login prompt and have all of the graphical menus and tools just like you'd expect at a
graphical console.  I've evaluated several packages, and these are the ones I like
best:
    eXcursion (by DEC, digital equipment corp, now Compaq)  May not be available for
download.
    PC-Xware by NCDsoft
    Xmanager by Netsarang
    Omni-X by (I forget who)
    X-Win32 by Starnet
Also, I don't know whether RedHat is configured by default to support an XDMCP
connection.  For that matter, I don't know if it's configured to support a simple
X-windows connection.



