21164 is indeed EV5 or EV56. Most people referred to EV56 as
21164A but Hudson preferred the much catchier "Digital Semiconductor
21164 (366MHz Through 433MHz) Alpha Microprocessor" - 
fairly trips off the tongue doesn't it.

I don't recall ho whigh EV56 went but 600MHz seems right -
I have at least one set of boxes running at 533MHz and they
were by no means the last EV56 boxes.

EV56 is not identical to EV5, though, there are a few
extra instructions (byte/word springs to mind but there
are others).

> EV67 is the same circuit as EV6, using the fab tech of EV7.
> So they wouldn't give it a new chip number, if the circuits are the same.

There was an EV68 on the roadmap too but I don't know how
EV6, EV67 and (maybe) EV68 have evolved. Docs for the first
two are available from the COMPAQ ftp site.

