Hmm, didn't realize that you used the pts filesystem. After some
experimenting
I found that it IS possible to telnet as root. Do not add pts/0...pts/9, but
only
the numbers, so your /etc/securetty looks something like:

tty1
tty2
...
tty8  # original
0      # your additions
1
2
...
9

So your terminal is actually a simple number, without the path.
You can use the pts pseudoterminal filesystem on other distributions as well
(you will of course have to make the same additions to /etc/securetty), but
only Redhat appears to install it automatically.

Good luck,

--
Martin Sinot
martin@nospam.spase.nl





