Ryan M Rafferty <rraffer1@osf1.gmu.edu> wrote:

> When I removed the SCSI card everything worked fine; unfortunately,
> this is the only NCR-based SCSI card I have

NCR aka Symbios aka LSI-based SCSI adapters are ubiquitously and
cheaply available from many vendors.  You should be able to pick
one up at the nearest computer chain store.  The PC164 firmware
recognizes those chips up to the 53C875.

> (and it is my understanding that only NCR-based cards will work
> for booting on PC164's).

SRM supports NCR and Qlogic.  ARC supports at least NCR and the
Adaptec 2940 series.  (Don't know about ARC and Qlogic.)  My PC164
came with a 2940W.

> Has anyone else had their PC164 boards get flaky after a while?

Mine hasn't.  (And while I have that machine only since a couple
of months ago, it's obviously a few years old judging from the SCSI
components it came with.)  I haven't heard about PC164s going bad
either, so it probably isn't a common problem.

-- 
Christian "naddy" Weisgerber                          naddy@mips.inka.de



