There are three most important applications when I use Alpha/Linux
(UP2000).

1. Scientific calculation with Compaq Fort.
2. LaTeXing 700-page documents (manuscript of my book)
3. Netscape

LaTexing unfortunately takes twice longer on Alpha/Linux
than on INtel/AMD/Linux around 800Mhz.

Because the Netscape was compiled with ccc under TruUnix
(by Compaq people), it starts as fast as it does under 
Intel/AMD linux. 

Scientific calculation is generally faster on Alpha/Linux
than on Intel/AMD/Linux at 800GHz.  Unfortunately my floating-point
application under Alpha/Linux does NOT run twice as fast as on 
Intel/AMD/Linux.

Two things should happen:
First, Compaq should release Fortran for Alpha/Linux that supports SMP 
right away.
Secondly, they should release CPUs faster than 1GHz in the marketplace
right away, not in their laboratory.

There are people who will buy an Alpha if it is cheaper than an
UltraSparc.
However, Without the above two things, people will lose interest in 
Alpha pretty quickly.

Regards,

HUgh


