About the kernel: we're of the opinion that since the kernel uses
all kinds of GNU extensions, trying to compile it just plain won't
work.  Even if it did work, the performance increase under normal
to medium load probably wouldn't be noticable since the kernel just
doesn't take up too much CPU time in the first place.

There is a slowly ongoing project to classify the standard installed
applications and libraries into those that can be compiled with ccc
and those that can't.  Check the newsgroup archives for lots of
progress reports over the last year.  We're not really dedicating
much of our time to the project since very few people seem to care.

