I'd still check out main memory.  Since the SX can't take ECC memory,
there's a increasing chance with the age of the DIMM that you can get
errors popping up.  See if changing out the memory helps.  New memory
is pretty cheap these days, maybe you could justify upgrading.

You could also try to reformat your swap, but I still think it's a
memory issue.  Init is just too simple to have a lot of pointers
flying around.  It also usually starts in the same spot in memory since
it's the first program that the kernel loads, so you may be hitting
the same bad bits.

Just my opinion,

Tony Hammitt


