PAL code is loaded at cold boot time by both whatever you are using for
BIOS and milo.  They're macro instructions for the processor, sort of the
great grandfather of Transmeta's programmable CPU.  If your PAL code is
corrupted, your machine may do all kinds of weird things.

You may try reinstalling your SRM or whatever (if it will let you) and
getting the latest milo version.  Check http://www.alphalinux.org

Any other opinions?


Tony Hammitt


